{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|は}}
{{IPAchar|/pa/}} → {{IPAchar|/ɸa/}} → {{IPAchar|/ha/}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|-}},<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref> from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*pa}}.

Probably cognate with {{cog|ojp|-}} verb {{ja-r|生ゆ|はゆ|to [[sprout]], to [[grow]]}} → modern {{ja-r|生える|はえる}}, and with {{ja-r|羽|は|[[feather]]; [[wing]]}}.

Suggested in some sources as possibly cognate with {{ja-r|歯|は|[[tooth]]}}, from the way that both sprout and then later fall,<ref>{{R:Gogen Yurai Jiten|葉／は|ha}}</ref> and with {{ja-r|刃|は|[[blade]]}} from similarities in shape (cf. {{cog|en|blade}}). However, the pitch accent patterns are different; {{m|ja|葉}} and {{m|ja|羽}} are both unaccented, while {{m|ja|歯}} and {{m|ja|刃}} are both accented. This may reflect two disparate ''*pa'' roots in the ancient language.

First attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 712 {{CE}} with the phonetic spelling {{lang|ja|波}}.<ref name="KDJ"/>

Cognate with {{cog|ryu|葉|tr=fā}}.

